    </Identification_Area>
    <Archive_Resource>
        <name>Mars Orbital Data Explorer</name>
        <version_id>1.0</version_id>
        <url>https://ode.rsl.wustl.edu/mars</url>
        <resource_type>Service</resource_type>
        <resource_subtype>Scientific Analysis Tool</resource_subtype>
        <resource_subtype>Search Tool</resource_subtype>
        <resource_subtype>Visualization Tool</resource_subtype>
        <resource_subtype>Web Application</resource_subtype>
        <interface_type>GUI Interface</interface_type>
        <description>The Mars Orbital Data Explorer (ODE) is a web-based tool that provides cross-mission and cross-instrument faceted product search, interactive map search, display, and download options for PDS data from major Mars orbital missions, including Mars Reconnaissance Orbiter, 2001 Mars Odyssey, Mars Global Surveyor, Viking Orbiters 1 and 2, and ESA’s Mars Express and ExoMars Trace Gas Orbiter. ODE includes a REST API for querying the ODE database from scripts, code, and other tools. A granular data system (GDS) supports retrieving subsets of point data from MGS MOLA products, with output in the form of CSV files, GIS shape files, and binned images.</description>
        <pds4_wide_applicability>false</pds4_wide_applicability>
    </Archive_Resource>
